The complete set of secure cookie attributes, extending Module 9, lesson 5's httpOnly:

app.use(session({
  secret: process.env.SESSION_SECRET,
  cookie: {
    httpOnly: true,      // Module 9's original flag - no JS access
    secure: true,        // cookie ONLY sent over HTTPS, never plain HTTP
    sameSite: 'strict',  // cookie NOT sent on cross-site requests at
                           // all - this is CSRF protection's first line
    maxAge: 60 * 60 * 1000
  }
}));

CSRF token verification for state-changing requests (a genuinely additional layer, beyond sameSite alone, for older browsers or specific scenarios):

import csrf from 'csurf';
const csrfProtection = csrf({ cookie: true });

app.get('/form', csrfProtection, (req, res) => {
  res.json({ csrfToken: req.csrfToken() }); // sent to the frontend,
                                               // included in the NEXT
                                               // state-changing request
});

app.post('/transfer-funds', csrfProtection, transferFundsHandler); // the
  // request must include the matching CSRF token, or it's rejected

Security headers, using a dedicated middleware:

import helmet from 'helmet';
app.use(helmet()); // sets several security-related headers automatically

