// PRODUCTION AUTH REVIEW - SaaS Application

// CHECK 1 - OAuth correctness: CONFIRMED - Google OAuth's code-for-token
// exchange happens entirely server-side, client secret read from env,
// and the app issues its own JWT afterward rather than storing Google's
// access token long-term.

// CHECK 2 - Token lifecycle: CONFIRMED via direct testing - reusing a
// refresh token a second time correctly fails with 401, verifying
// genuine rotation, not just code review of the rotation logic.

// CHECK 3 - Permission granularity: FOUND a genuine gap during the
// permission-matrix audit - the 'support' role was accidentally granted
// 'billing:manage' permission, which should be admin-only. This was
// never caught by individual route testing, only by the explicit,
// exhaustive matrix audit lesson 3 recommended.
// FINDING: Remove 'billing:manage' from the support role immediately.

// CHECK 4 - MFA independence: FOUND a genuine CROSS-MECHANISM gap -
// MFA verification assumes every user has a locally-stored password to
// check first (stage 1), but OAuth-authenticated users have NO local
// password at all. MFA-enabled OAuth users are currently being silently
// SKIPPED past MFA entirely, since stage 1's password check fails to
// even apply meaningfully to them.
// FINDING: MFA's stage 1 must be adapted to recognize OAuth-authenticated
// users (who've already proven identity via lesson 1's flow) and proceed
// directly to stage 2's MFA check for them specifically, rather than
// either failing or silently skipping MFA for this entire user category.

// CHECK 5 - Surface hardening: CONFIRMED via direct header inspection -
// helmet's headers are genuinely present, and CSRF protection is
// correctly applied to /refresh specifically (since it's a genuinely
// state-changing endpoint), not just to obviously sensitive routes.

// VERDICT: Checks 1, 2, and 5 passed with genuine verification. Check 3
// found a real permission gap. Check 4 found a genuine CROSS-MECHANISM
// integration gap (OAuth + MFA interaction) that no single mechanism's
// own isolated testing would ever have revealed.
